# InterGenOS systemd preset — the Chronicle backup engine.
# The package's post_install enables and starts these on install, but the
# installer's services phase runs `systemctl --root <target> preset-all`
# AFTER the package hooks, and the image-wide default-disable preset then
# strips any unit no preset whitelists — measured on the ge9b-12 installed
# system: the hook-created enablement links for chronicled.service and all
# three timers were removed by preset-all and the engine sat dead on first
# boot. Real-distro pattern (same as gdm): the package ships its own preset
# so preset-all wires it rather than un-wiring it.
enable chronicled.service
enable chronicle-userdata.timer
enable chronicle-offpeak.timer
enable chronicle-scrub.timer
